notes/prior_art_map.md:264:- **Mechanism/hypotheses:** Elliptic-curve division polynomials compactly produce integers divisible by many primes; the smoothness conjecture controls coverage.
notes/prior_art_map.md:437:- **Primitive/relevance:** A rigorously computable order-threshold certificate or factor. It does not supply exact large orders or informative dual-lattice samples in polynomial time in \(n\).
notes/prior_art_map.md:475:- **Result:** Sections 3–4 give an explicit heuristic smoothness-candidate generator and computational comparisons; no theorem there proves a new general factoring exponent.
notes/prior_art_map.md:476:- **Mechanism:** Chinese remaindering expresses candidates as subsums satisfying selected small-prime divisibility constraints. Search for small representatives relative to the selected modulus, then test residual smoothness and perform ordinary relation processing.
notes/prior_art_map.md:477:- **Hypotheses:** Practical smoothness behavior and parameter choices; modular roots concern known factor-base primes.
notes/prior_art_map.md:523:## 36. Pollard \(p-1\): smooth order as sufficient partial structure
notes/prior_art_map.md:547:- **Representation/hypotheses:** Odd RSA factors permit inversion modulo \(2^t\). A two-dimensional lattice contains \((q_1,q_2)\); Gauss reduction and the stronger inequality give the rigorous result.
notes/prior_art_map.md:549:- **Primitive/relevance:** A concrete correlated-information format that suffices without revealing the common bit string. The rigorous two-modulus regime is substantially unbalanced; do not transfer it to two ordinary balanced RSA moduli. **VERIFIED.**
