I found a concrete issue in the paper’s stronger DCH statement: it includes square inputs but excludes \(A=B\). For \(N=s^2\) and candidate \(p=s\), the expression is \((B-A)s^2\), so no band prime larger than \(H\) can divide it. D′ is unaffected, but that conjecture is false as written.

There is also a population issue: under ordinary counting over all semiprimes, Pollard–Strassen already factors a \(1-o(1)\) fraction within \(N^{1/6+o(1)}\). The meaningful extension is a guarantee uniform in ratio bands.
