Let M be a prime with M ∤ 2ABN, and let r be a root of Br² ≡ AN (mod M). Write s = N·r^{−1}
(mod M²; the inverse is taken mod M², as codex points out). Then for every integer
p ≡ r (mod M) with q = N/p ∈ Z:

  Bp + Aq ≡ c := Br + As (mod M²).

